==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sent- (feel)}}
From {{bor|en|la|sentiēns||feeling, perceiving}}, present active participle of {{m|la|sentiō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛn.ti.ənt/|a=UK}}<ref name=Cambridge>{{cite-web|titleurl=https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/english/sentient|title=SENTIENT {{!}} Pronunciation in English|publisher=Cambridge University Press|accessdate=2020-09-18}}</ref>
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sentient.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛn.ʃ(i.)ənt/|a=US}}<ref name=Cambridge/>

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Experiencing [[sensation]], [[thought]], or [[feeling]].
#: {{syn|en|sensate}}
# Able to consciously [[perceive]] through the use of [[sense]] faculties.
#: {{ant|en|insensate}}
# {{lb|en|loosely|chiefly|science fiction}} Possessing human-like awareness and intelligence.
#: {{syn|en|sapient|Thesaurus:self-aware}}
#* {{quote-av|en|episode={{w|Silent Enemy (Star Trek: Enterprise)|Silent Enemy}}|title=Star Trek: Enterprise|season=1|number=12|year=2002|writer=w:André Bormanis|role=w:Jonathan Archer|passage=Not even a microbe? I don't want to blow up something that could evolve into a '''sentient''' species in a couple of billion years.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/14/labelling-googles-lamda-chatbot-as-sentient-is-fanciful-but-its-very-human-to-be-taken-in-by-machines|title=Labelling Google’s LaMDA chatbot as sentient is fanciful. But it’s very human to be taken in by machines|author=w:Toby Walsh|date=2022-06-14|work=The Guardian|passage=Lemoine has been placed on “paid administrative leave” after publishing a transcript of conversations with LaMDA which he claims support his belief that the chatbot is '''sentient''' and comparable to a seven- or eight-year-old child. {{...}} While Lemoine no doubt genuinely believes his claims, LaMDA is likely to be as '''sentient''' as a traffic light.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Cade Metz|title=A.I. Is Not Sentient. Why Do People Say It Is?|work=The New York Times|date=2022-08-05|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/05/technology/ai-sentient-google.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=After more than 25 years as an artificial intelligence researcher{{...|–a quarter-century spent in pursuit of a machine that could think like a human—}}Dr. Goertzel knew he had finally reached the end goal: Desdemona, a machine he had built, was '''sentient'''. But a few minutes later, he realized this was nonsense.}}

